.TH QUADRF-HOTSPOT 8 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-hotspot \- fallback Wi-Fi access point for a QuadRF appliance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-hotspot
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waits up to twelve seconds for wlan0 to associate with a saved network and
pick up an address. If it does, the script removes any access point DNS
configuration and exits, leaving the appliance in station mode.
.PP
Otherwise it takes wlan0 away from wpa_supplicant, gives it
.BR QUADRF_AP_ADDRESS ,
starts hostapd with
.B QUADRF_AP_SSID
(an open network: hostapd
.BR wpa=0 ,
no password)
and isc-dhcp-server for leases, and publishes
.BR quadrf.local
on wlan0. Wildcard DNS
.RB ( address=/#/ )
is not used: it is global in dnsmasq and would hijack names on eth0 and usb0
while the AP is up.
.PP
.B quadrf-hotspot.service
runs this once at boot. The script exits with an error if
.B dtoverlay=disable-wifi
is present in the firmware configuration, since wlan0 will not exist;
.B quadrf-boot
removes that line, but the change needs a reboot.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dnsmasq.d/quadrf-wlan0-ap.conf
Captive DNS while the access point is up.
.TP
.I /etc/hostapd/quadrf.conf
Generated from
.B QUADRF_AP_SSID
by
.BR "quadrf apply" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1),
.BR quadrf.conf (5),
.BR quadrf-dns-update (8),
.BR quadrf-ethernet (8),
.BR quadrf-usb (8)
